🚀 My Top 10 Tools as an AWS DevOps Engineer (That I am using on Day-to-day basis)

1️⃣ Terraform 🏗️
I use Terraform to create AWS infrastructure with code.
 No manual setup — just one command and your cloud is ready!

2️⃣ Git / GitHub 🧠
This is how I track and manage every change in code.
 Git helps me go back in time if something breaks. GitHub makes teamwork easy.

3️⃣ Azure DevOps 🛠️
I use it to run CI/CD pipelines and manage tasks.
 Even in AWS projects, Azure DevOps helps keep things organized and automated.

4️⃣ AWS Health Dashboard 🚨
Before AWS has issues, this dashboard tells me!
 It shows me problems in AWS services early — so I can plan and stay ahead.

5️⃣ CloudWatch 🔍
This is my go-to tool for logs and alerts.
 If something crashes or slows down, I check CloudWatch first.

6️⃣ Docker 🐳
I use Docker to run apps the same way everywhere — laptop or cloud.
 It helps me avoid the “it works on my machine” problem.

7️⃣ RDS (Relational Database Service) 💾
RDS runs my SQL databases without me worrying about setup, backups, or scaling.
 AWS takes care of it — I just focus on performance.

8️⃣ DynamoDB ⚡
For fast, NoSQL database needs, I use DynamoDB.
 It handles huge traffic and still stays super fast!

9️⃣ AWS Secrets Manager 🔐
This tool keeps passwords and secrets safe.
 No more storing secrets in code — it's secure and smart.

🔟 SQS (Simple Queue Service) 📬
SQS helps me connect different services using message queues.
 If one service is slow or down, others still keep working smoothly.
